digraph circuit_design {
    graph [
        goal="Design an electronic circuit that satisfies the user request.",
        rankdir=LR,
        default_max_retry="2",
        model_stylesheet="
            * { llm_model: claude-sonnet-4.6; llm_provider: anthropic; }
        "
    ]

    start [shape=Mdiamond, label="Start"]
    exit  [shape=Msquare, label="Exit"]

    define_requirements [
        shape=box,
        auto_status=true,
        prompt="Goal: $goal

Create a concise engineering requirements document for this circuit request.

Read any relevant repo docs first if they exist. Write the result to:
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/circuit_requirements.md

The requirements document must include:
- the functional behavior implied by the goal, with quantitative acceptance criteria where possible
- operating assumptions for the power source and environment implied by the goal
- output/load assumptions, including current, voltage, timing, and tolerance constraints as applicable
- component constraints, including preference for widely available parts and simple topology
- a verification plan that can be checked later without ambiguity

Keep the document under 250 lines. Be concrete and quantitative.

Write to $KILROY_STAGE_STATUS_PATH (fallback: $KILROY_STAGE_STATUS_FALLBACK_PATH) ONLY on failure:
{\"status\":\"fail\",\"failure_reason\":\"...\",\"failure_class\":\"deterministic\"}"
    ]

    choose_topology [
        shape=box,
        auto_status=true,
        prompt="Goal: $goal

Read:
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/circuit_requirements.md

Choose a practical circuit topology for this request and justify it. Prefer a robust, easy-to-build design over novelty.

Write these artifacts:
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/topology_decision.md
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/preliminary_bom.md

The topology decision must cover:
- the core circuit approach and why it is suitable for the goal
- whether regulation, filtering, reverse-polarity protection, and transient suppression are needed
- every major component and its role
- the key sizing logic for component values, including timing or load-drive calculations when relevant
- any design risks or assumptions that should be reviewed later

The BOM must list one component per line with reference designator class, suggested part, and purpose.

Write to $KILROY_STAGE_STATUS_PATH (fallback: $KILROY_STAGE_STATUS_FALLBACK_PATH) ONLY on failure:
{\"status\":\"fail\",\"failure_reason\":\"...\",\"failure_class\":\"deterministic\"}"
    ]

    produce_design [
        shape=box,
        auto_status=true,
        prompt="Goal: $goal

Read:
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/circuit_requirements.md
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/topology_decision.md
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/preliminary_bom.md

Produce the actual circuit design artifacts for this request.

Write:
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/circuit_design.md
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/final_bom.csv
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/schematic_notes.md

Requirements for circuit_design.md:
- describe the full circuit in clear implementation order
- name all nodes and key component values
- include the calculations needed to justify the design, such as timing, biasing, gain, filtering, or current-limit calculations as applicable
- describe input protection, decoupling, and environmental robustness choices appropriate to the goal
- include assembly notes and expected behavior at startup

Requirements for final_bom.csv:
- header row: item,designator,part,value_or_package,purpose
- one component per row

Requirements for schematic_notes.md:
- textual net-by-net connection notes sufficient for a human to draw the schematic
- include polarity-sensitive parts and orientation notes

Do not leave placeholders. If a value is estimated, say so explicitly and keep it realistic.

Write to $KILROY_STAGE_STATUS_PATH (fallback: $KILROY_STAGE_STATUS_FALLBACK_PATH) ONLY on failure:
{\"status\":\"fail\",\"failure_reason\":\"...\",\"failure_class\":\"deterministic\"}"
    ]

    review_design [
        shape=box,
        auto_status=true,
        prompt="Goal: $goal

Read:
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/circuit_requirements.md
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/topology_decision.md
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/preliminary_bom.md
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/circuit_design.md
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/final_bom.csv
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/schematic_notes.md

Review the design critically as if preparing it for implementation.

Write:
- .ai/runs/$KILROY_RUN_ID/design_review.md

The review must explicitly check:
- whether the design satisfies the stated goal and acceptance criteria
- correctness of the main sizing and component-selection logic
- power-input and environment concerns implied by the requirements
- whether the artifacts are complete enough for a human to build the circuit

If the design is inadequate, write a failure status with a specific reason. If it is acceptable, write the review and exit normally.

Write to $KILROY_STAGE_STATUS_PATH (fallback: $KILROY_STAGE_STATUS_FALLBACK_PATH) ONLY on failure:
{\"status\":\"fail\",\"failure_reason\":\"design review found a blocking issue\",\"failure_class\":\"deterministic\"}"
    ]

    start -> define_requirements
    define_requirements -> choose_topology
    choose_topology -> produce_design
    produce_design -> review_design
    review_design -> exit
}
